{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And you shall sow the eighth year, etc.</b> It was necessary to say this, for since He said ״וְעָשָׂת אֶת הַתְּבוּאָה לִשְׁלֹשׁ הַשָּׁנִים״, one might have supposed that a person would say: if the eighth year is fit for sowing, why should a miracle be performed so that the produce of the sixth year suffices for the eighth? Therefore Scripture states explicitly ״וּזְרַעְתֶּם אֵת הַשָּׁנָה הַשְּׁמִינִית״, and it gives the reason for the blessing of the sixth year's produce sufficing for the eighth year — it is on account of ״וַאֲכַלְתֶּם מִן הַתְּבוּאָה יָשָׁן״, so that you eat in the eighth year from old produce and not new, for old produce is healthier for people than new (Bava Batra 91a), as is known. And as a father has compassion upon his children, so may HaShem have compassion upon His people."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:01:15.918692216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}